### Source statement: turn the Ubuntu test run on regardless; an internal Ubuntu CI is separable [SRC-PUB-UBUNTU-CI-LINE]

- part-of: [SRC-PUB-STATEMENTS]
- source-text: Practically speaking, I am only running gnomon on MacOS. I am willing to invest so that Gnomon is Ubuntu-compatible, but until we have a sizable number of third party users, I don't have an objection to Ubuntu bugs surfacing at release time. We should turn it on regardless, because it validates Ubuntu compatibility at no cost. Whether we build out an Ubuntu ci/cd separately internally to validate builds first is a separate/severable decision.
- source-locator: the maintainer's message of 2026-11-20, 19:08:28Z, received by remote control and copied by program by the development-model owner
