- x-d1: D1 [DD-PUB-VOCAB-AS-CI-SECRET] serves G4 through R6; [DD-PUB-SCRIPT-FIRST] bounds when D1 and T4 apply, which is the later private-repository job.
- x-trace-rule: Every requirement here traces to a goal and every goal to at least one test; nothing in this file traces to no goal.
- x-other: [DD-PUB-RELEASE-TOOLING-LATER] bounds G1's scope and carries no requirement.

## Plan: steps 1 and 2a are built; the rest follows [PLAN-PUB]

- part-of: [FL-PUBLICATION]
- status: draft
- x-state: Steps 1 and 2a are built: (1) the scanner's publication mode (R1, R2, R6, R7), merged; (2a) the snapshot builder with the folder map and the release-prep script, dry-run against a scratch bare repository only (R3, R4, R8, R11, R12; T7, T8, T11), both in review, not yet merged. Still to build: (2b) the public test set (R10; T10); (3) the public workflow file under the map (R9; T9), which no longer waits on the maintainer's answer, because he confirmed on 2026-11-22 that the Ubuntu decision covers this project ([SRC-PUB-UBUNTU-CI-BOTH-LINE]); (4) the first release, at the maintainer's gate, then T12 once the first push-triggered public run exists. The private-repository CI job (D1, D5, T4, T5) follows later. T1a, T1b, T2, T3 and T6 are shown red first, as [ACC-PUB] requires.

## Requirement: an unconfigured run in a lenient mode says so and never looks like a clean run [REQ-PUB-UNCONFIGURED-SAYS-SO]

- part-of: [FL-PUBLICATION]
- status: draft
- x-label: R7
- implements: [GOAL-PUB-NO-SILENT-UNCONFIGURED]
- verified-by: [SCEN-PUB-UNCONFIGURED-NOT-CLEAN]
- see-also: [DD-PUB-FAIL-CLOSED-IN-PUBLICATION-MODE]
- x-rule: Outside publication mode, a run in which a private file is missing or empty does not print a zero-findings result. It says which private file was not loaded and that its rules were not checked. It may exit 0. Its output and the output of a configured run that found nothing are never the same.
- x-present-gap: Before this requirement, such a run warns that a private file is missing but still prints a zero-findings result.
- x-whose: A ruling of 2026-11-19 by the owner of the development model, who is not the maintainer: the lenient modes stay lenient, and an unconfigured run and a clean run must never look the same.
